{"id": "EUVD-2026-103522", "enisaUuid": "4d1ac6eb-8869-3f13-b2c2-eac110c8adf2", "description": "librtmp in RTMPDump through 2.6 contains an out-of-bounds read and heap out-of-bounds write vulnerability because AMF3_Decode ignores AMF3 property decode failures. Malicious RTMP servers or man-in-the-middle attackers can send oversized AMF3 string lengths, and with the token option DecodeTEA corrupts heap memory and leaks heap bytes.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T12:19:50", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T16:12:27", "baseScore": 6.1, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:P/PR:N/UI:P/VC:L/VI:L/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://hackmd.io/@haindpwn/librtmp-amf3-decode-and-strict-array-oob", "https://git.ffmpeg.org/gitweb/rtmpdump.git/blob/138fdb258d9fc26f1843fd1b891180416c9dc575:/librtmp/amf.c", "https://rtmpdump.mplayerhq.hu/", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/librtmp-rtmpdump-through-2.6-heap-out-of-bounds-write-via-amf3-decode"], "aliases": ["GHSA-x953-qc42-3hqh", "CVE-2026-112060"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "3552eeae-db95-3b8c-a2ea-d52ca8e493f9", "product": {"name": "librtmp", "vendor": {"name": "RTMPDump"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22642.6"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8a03d33b-a050-3eb6-92a2-378c99bfefa3", "vendor": {"name": "RTMPDump"}}], "isExploited": false}